# Do-not-touch — protected core

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` (the dispatch/notify engine) and `app/src/types.ts` (the
core types + `Action` union) are load-bearing — see
`materials/architecture-brief.md`. Every other file in `app/src` depends on
their shape. This rule is `alwaysApply: true` because it must hold regardless
of which other rules are attached.

## Rule

- Do **not** edit `app/src/store.ts` at all unless the user explicitly asks
  for a store-engine change. Feature work never requires touching it.
- Do **not** remove or rename existing fields/members of `AppState`, `Task`,
  or existing `Action` union variants in `app/src/types.ts`. **Additive**
  changes (a new `Action` variant, a new optional-safe `Task` field with a
  default) are allowed as part of normal feature work.
- If a task seems to require breaking either rule, stop and ask instead of
  proceeding.

## How to verify

1. `git diff -- app/src/store.ts` is empty unless the user explicitly approved
   a store-engine change.
2. `git diff -- app/src/types.ts` (if any) only **adds** lines — no existing
   field or union member was deleted or renamed.
